here’s the code with random 3D transforms on the `.background-container` - it’ll tumble in space on load, with separate rotations for x, y, and z axes. i kept the text and icon in place relative to the container so they stay attached while it spins. the `perspective` on the body makes the 3D effect pop, and the `transform-style: preserve-3d` keeps the depth intact.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
	<style>
body {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: center;
  align-items: center;
  height: 10vh;
  margin: 0;
  overflow: hidden;
  perspective: 1000px; /* adds depth to 3D space */
}

.background-container {
  position: absolute;
  width: 10em;
  height: 10em;
  transition: transform 0.5s ease;
  transform-style: preserve-3d;
}

.background {
  position: relative;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  display: flex;
  justify-content: center;
  align-items: center;
  backface-visibility: hidden; /* hides back side when flipped */
}

.background-icon-container {
  position: absolute;
  height: 100%;
  width: 100%;
  display: flex;
  justify-content: center;
  align-items: center;
}

.background-icon {
  font-size: 5em;
  transform: translateZ(10px); /* slight depth */
}

.background-text-container {
  position: absolute;
  top: 50%;
  left: 50%;
  transform: translate(-50%, -50%) translateZ(5px); /* depth for text */
  max-width: 90%;
  max-height: 90%;
  white-space: nowrap;
  text-align: center;
  color: white;
  text-shadow: 1px 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,0.5);
}

.background-text {
  font-size: 1.5em;
  line-height: 1.1em;
}
	</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="background-container" id="backgroundContainer">
  <div class="background">
    <div class="background-icon-container">
      <span class="background-icon">🇬🇧</span>
    </div>
    <div class="background-text-container">
      <span class="background-text">YES, WE CARE!</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<script>
  const container = document.getElementById('backgroundContainer');

  // randomize position and 3D rotation on all axes
  container.style.left = `${Math.floor(Math.random() * (window.innerWidth - 100))}px`;
  container.style.top = `${Math.floor(Math.random() * (window.innerHeight - 100))}px`;

  const rotateX = Math.floor(Math.random() * 180 - 90);
  const rotateY = Math.floor(Math.random() * 180 - 90);
  const rotateZ = Math.floor(Math.random() * 180 - 90);

  container.style.transform = `
    rotateX(${rotateX}deg)
    rotateY(${rotateY}deg)
    rotateZ(${rotateZ}deg)
  `;
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

the container now spins randomly on all three axes - x (tilt), y (swing), and z (spin). if you wanna tweak how wild the rotation gets, just adjust the `180` in the `Math.random()` calls. or if you want the text to react differently to the 3D space, i can mess with the `translateZ` values. want me to add a bit of physics to the randomness, like making it spin longer on one axis?

