To print a received SMS to the screen, you need a BroadcastReceiver to listen for the SMS intent and a way to update your UI.

First, add these permissions to your AndroidManifest.xml:

```xml
<uses-permission android:name="android.permission.RECEIVE_SMS" />
<uses-permission android:name="android.permission.READ_SMS" />
```

Then, create the BroadcastReceiver in Java:

```java
public class SmsReceiver extends BroadcastReceiver {
    @Override
    public void onReceive(Context context, Intent intent) {
        Bundle bundle = intent.getExtras();
        if (bundle != null) {
            Object[] pdus = (Object[]) bundle.get("pdus");
            if (pdus != null) {
                for (Object pdu : pdus) {
                    SmsMessage smsMessage = SmsMessage.createFromPdu((byte[]) pdu);
                    String sender = smsMessage.getDisplayOriginatingAddress();
                    String messageBody = smsMessage.getMessageBody();

                    String fullText = "From: " + sender + "\nMsg: " + messageBody;

                    Toast.makeText(context, fullText, Toast.LENGTH_LONG).show();
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
```

Register the receiver in your AndroidManifest.xml:

```xml
<receiver android:name=".SmsReceiver" android:permission="android.permission.BROADCAST_SMS">
    <intent-filter>
        <action android:name="android.provider.Telephony.SMS_RECEIVED" />
    </intent-filter>
</receiver>
```

Note: For Android 6.0+, you must request the RECEIVE_SMS permission at runtime using ActivityCompat.requestPermissions before this will work.

